==Question #11==
{{Cquote2|Can you buff some of the daily achievement diary rewards? For example, wilderness elite diary lets you claim 50 free runes per day from Lundail. It's so bad; you can get 50 air runes.}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7rV3iLITLmU&t=2405s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Kirby:''' Some of those diaries' rewards are wild.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' I feel like, over the last five years, we've very slowly increased the number of teleports that you get from different tiers. Some of them we haven't hit at all, some of them we've fixed and made better, but there's no consistency in them and some of the rewards they're just pointless; they may as well not exist, I complete a diary, and I go "oh I'm excited, what do I get? Oh, the only thing I care about is the XP lamp".
* '''Mod Kieren:''' To be honest, It's not just the rewards; some of these could just be buffed; the teleport should probably be always unlimited at the elite level; I think some of them are unlimited straight away, you know you get the Ardougne medium cape you've got the unlimited teleports to the monastery, I don't want to take that away from people, but they need looking at, some of them are just really weak. Even the achievement diaries beyond that, having played my group Ironman recently, gives you a fresh perspective when you experience all the diaries and stuff again; you really realise how many diaries require you to plant a palm tree; it's so many. You realise how many diaries have the exact same requirements; there's a bunch of diaries that all require 70 Prayer, there's a bunch of diaries that all require around 70ish Smithing as well. We've got 23 skills, we could spread this out better, make them more fitting to the content that is in the area and so on, but that brings in a much bigger conversation around reworking the task lists of diaries, which is complicated because we already have diaries out, some people have got the rewards and so on.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' This kind of brings me on to another point. We released the Lumbridge Diary years ago; maybe in 2015, new content comes out, and it's never represented in the diaries. It probably should be, right? This diary is a really good way for players to find out some of the content that is in those areas, so I quite like the idea of reviewing the diary tasks for all of the diaries, and that might even mean removing some of the tasks, or replacing with something more fitting for those areas, or adding diversity, so you don't have the same task in multiple diaries because that's a bit rubbish, Even on the requirements front, to try and have some diversity and requirements so that you're not blocked by Runecrafting in every single diary for instance, and also maybe we start the precedent of adding new tasks to the diaries over time. Let's say we add Tempoross; it should probably be represented in the desert diary in some capacity. How do we handle that? That is an interesting topic because nobody likes using the rewards. So how do you tackle it? How do you bring in Tempoross in a task that is gonna make the diary complete, but also not frustrate everybody because you constantly have to come back every month and do another task since the requirements would slowly creep up? It's something to think about.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' The other thing that we've talked about briefly on the odd occasion is a master-level diary. Imagine we do these touch-ups review a bunch of the tasks. Then you also have a new master tier that's not on one diary; it's across the whole world, "The Master Gielinor Diary" or something like that, where we can push the higher end and add a new level of achievement diary tasks. It could be a little bit more than just planetary; think combat achievements, obviously, not combat focus necessarily, or you might have some time-based challenges or things like that. I'm not necessarily committed to that kind of approach, but I'm sort of imagining that they can all come together as some more, big, cohesive achievement diary refresh.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' With combat achievements, we have actually set a precedent where we can just add tasks, and if we go back through achievement diaries regularly, we can actually upgrade the interfaces because the combat achievement ones are so much nicer, so there's definitely scope to do a decent-sized project on that.
* '''Mod Kieren:''' Yeah, the interfaces are questionable
* '''Mod Kirby:'''  Yes, our interface work has come on significantly since 2015. There are the buttons on the player panel where you click on the achievement diary and you get a little scroll, you click on the combat achievements when you get this massive one where you can go through the world and click on individual bosses, and it just works.
* '''Mod Bruno:''' I like the tab for the achievements diaries themselves, especially after the update where you get a little bit more on the bar for every task you do, but it feels weird that you open the diary, and it's this quest log looking thing from like 2005.
